    <record id="channel_records_s1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_records" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Clients and treatment plans</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_records_s1_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_records" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Bringing on a client</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Someone becomes a client the moment you tick <strong>Is a Client</strong>, whether they booked online or you're entering them after a consultation. Open <span class="oe-path">Practice › Clients › New</span>, or find them under Contacts and tick the box: a <strong>Client #</strong> is assigned automatically.</p><p>On the <strong>Client</strong> tab, fill in date of birth, emergency contact and referring provider. Under <strong>Before Treating</strong>, add the <strong>Health Flags</strong> that apply and any allergies, so every practitioner sees them before a session.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/practice_elearning/static/img/client_form.png" alt="A client's record with health flags" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a client's Client tab, with a health flag and an allergy recorded.</p></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-flag" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Your own health flags</span><p>Each practice keeps its own list in <span class="oe-path">Practice › Configuration › Health Flags</span>: for example Pregnant, Blood thinners or Recent injury.</p></div></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-globe" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Requested online?</span><p>A client who requests an appointment on your website is flagged and numbered automatically too. Fill in their health details at the first visit.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_records_s1_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_records" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">The treatment plan</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Everything that follows, consent, pre-treatment tests and sessions, hangs off a <strong>treatment plan</strong>: one per thing you're treating the client for. Choose the <strong>Treatment</strong> from your practice's list, add the <strong>Area / Focus</strong>, and set yourself as <strong>Primary Practitioner</strong>.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><div class="oe-flow"><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-inbox" /></span>Intake</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-heartbeat" /></span>In Treatment</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-check" /></span>Completed</div></div></div><p>Move the plan's status as you start, and again when it's done (or Discontinued).</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/practice_elearning/static/img/plan_form.png" alt="A treatment plan" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a treatment plan, with the tabs the rest of this course uses.</p></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-list" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Your own treatments</span><p>Set up what your practice treats in <span class="oe-path">Practice › Configuration › Treatment Types</span>: "Deep tissue for back pain", "Sleep support", "Strength program"... Rename the starting "General treatment" to suit.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_records_s2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_records" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Consent and pre-treatment tests</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">22</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_records_s2_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_records" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Consent</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">23</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>One record per consent: treatment, pre-treatment test or photo release. Add a row on the plan's <strong>Consents</strong> tab; the <strong>Form</strong> fills in with your wording for that kind.</p><p>Print it from the record's <span class="oe-path">Print</span> menu, have the client sign, then click <strong>Mark Signed</strong>.</p><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-pencil" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Your own wording</span><p>Edit the forms, or add your own, in <span class="oe-path">Practice › Configuration › Consent Forms</span>. The first form of each kind is used for new consents.</p></div></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-camera" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Photos are separate</span><p>A photo release is its own consent: a client can say yes to treatment and no to photos. A printed but unsigned consent doesn't count.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_records_s2_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_records" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Pre-treatment tests</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">24</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>A check before treatment starts, such as a skin patch test for an oil or remedy, or a fitness assessment. Add a row on the plan's <strong>Pre-treatment Tests</strong> tab: the test, what was tested and its lot number, and the date. <strong>Read On</strong> fills in from the test type's waiting time.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><div class="oe-flow"><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-eyedropper" /></span>Done today</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-clock-o" /></span>Read on the date</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-check-circle" /></span>Clear, or Reaction / Concern</div></div></div><p>Record the result with notes when you check it. Tests to read show on My Day.</p><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-refresh" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Only the latest counts</span><p>A new clear test replaces an old one. Set up your tests and their waiting times in <span class="oe-path">Practice › Configuration › Pre-treatment Test Types</span>.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_records_s3" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_records" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Documenting a session</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">34</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_records_s3_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_records" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Documenting a session</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">35</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>A session is created for you when you complete an appointment, or you can add one on the plan's <strong>Sessions</strong> tab. Record the products used and their lot numbers, the area or focus, your session notes, and whether aftercare was given.</p><p>Add before and after photos; sessions on a plan are numbered in date order, so progress is easy to follow. Set <strong>Next Session Recommended</strong> and My Day reminds you to book it.</p><div class="oe-callout oe-callout-warning"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">If something went wrong</span><p>Tick <strong>Reaction or Concern</strong> and describe it.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
