    <record id="channel_scheduling_s1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_scheduling" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">One-time setup</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_scheduling_s1_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_scheduling" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Adding yourself as a practitioner</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Open <span class="oe-path">Practice › Configuration › Practitioners › New</span> and set <strong>User</strong> to your own login. Click into <strong>Working Hours</strong> to set the days and times you work: the booking page uses them to know when you're free, and time off you add there is respected.</p><p>Add your licence or certification number while you're there.</p><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-key" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">One thing to know</span><p>Creating or editing a Working Hours calendar needs Administrator access. Adding a practitioner later who isn't an Administrator? Set their hours up for them the first time.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_scheduling_s1_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_scheduling" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Your services, and the checks that come first</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>In <span class="oe-path">Practice › Configuration › Services</span>, add one row per thing you offer, with its <strong>Duration</strong> and a <strong>Buffer After</strong> for cleanup or notes. Tick <strong>Bookable Online</strong> for anything a client may request themselves, often just a consultation or a first visit.</p><p>A service can require a <strong>clear pre-treatment test</strong> and a <strong>signed treatment consent</strong> before it can be booked, and can <strong>create a session</strong> record when it's completed.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/practice_elearning/static/img/service_form.png" alt="A service with its requirements" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a treatment session that needs a clear test and signed consent first.</p></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-shield" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">What the requirements do</span><p>A service with requirements can't be booked, by you or online, against a treatment plan until the plan meets them. Nothing gets booked ahead of the safety step.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_scheduling_s2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_scheduling" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Booking appointments</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">22</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_scheduling_s2_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_scheduling" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Booking one yourself, and confirming a request</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">23</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p><strong>Booking it yourself:</strong> <span class="oe-path">Practice › Appointments › New</span>: pick the client, the service and, for a service with requirements, the treatment plan it's for. The end time comes from the service's duration and buffer, and you can't double-book yourself.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/practice_elearning/static/img/appointment_new.png" alt="A new appointment" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>booking an appointment.</p></div><p><strong>Confirming a web request:</strong> open <span class="oe-path">Practice › Records › Needs Confirmation</span>, check it and click <strong>Confirm</strong>: the client gets a confirmation email.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><div class="oe-flow"><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-user-times" /></span>No-show</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-ban" /></span>Cancel</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-check" /></span>Complete</div></div></div><p>Complete creates the linked session record for you, ready for your notes.</p></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_scheduling_s2_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_scheduling" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">The client's own online booking</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">24</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><div class="oe-diagram"><div class="oe-flow"><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-list" /></span>Pick a service</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-calendar" /></span>Real open times</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-inbox" /></span>Lands in Needs Confirmation</div></div></div><p>A client only ever sees services marked <strong>Bookable Online</strong>.</p><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-lock" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Services with requirements stay hidden until they're met</span><p>They only show once the client has a treatment plan that meets them. A brand-new client sees a consultation, not a treatment, until you've seen them and opened a plan. Nothing from their records is shown online.</p></div></div><p>Clients can cancel their own upcoming appointment, but only more than 24 hours ahead.</p></div></field>
    </record>
